		{"id":"12b34769a0056e28","type":"text","text":"fxaa as a render setting requires a scratch buffer present in the FrameBuffer\n\nAnd the check may not be done very efficiently with the type system when whether a scratch buffer is needed depends on a runtime setting","x":-476,"y":1044,"width":250,"height":236,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d020ca0ae53be225","type":"text","text":"```python\nclass Simple2DRenderables(Renderable):\n\trender_shape: Callable[[RenderTriangle, FrameBuffer], FrameBuffer] = default_simple2d_render_func\n\tdef triangulate(self) -> list[RenderTriangle]:\n\t\t...\n\t\n\t@override\n\tdef redner_to(self, buf: FrameBuffer) -> FrameBuffer:\n\t\treturn self.render_shape(self.triangulate(), buf)\n\t\n```","x":-883,"y":1700,"width":763,"height":280},
